[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Version=1.0
Name=Cachy-Void updater (tray)
Comment=Quietly notice when updates, or a kernel waiting for its first boot, need you
# NOT gated with OnlyShowIn/NotShowIn, and that is the point. Every applier the
# branding writes IS gated, because a look belongs to one desktop; this is the
# product's own status surface and belongs in whichever session the user picked.
# The bare-Openbox session reads no XDG autostart at all, so cachy-branding adds
# its line to ~/.config/openbox/autostart instead - exactly one mechanism per
# session, never two (the nm-tray double-icon lesson).
Exec=cachy-updater-tray
Icon=/usr/share/cachy-void/branding/void-cachy-updater.svg
Terminal=false
NoDisplay=true
X-GNOME-Autostart-enabled=true
Categories=System;Settings;
